<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-002-AO24>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-002-AO24" ;
  triage:title "Deliverable 4 negative pre-router mTLS-auth-rejection evidence unimplemented" ;
  triage:description "Deliverable 4 requires 'negative pre-router authentication evidence' as part of the bidirectional M4<->M5 proof -- i.e. a live connection rejected before HTTP decode/router entry. No such mechanism exists anywhere in scripts/smoke/: run_feature_smoke.py's curl_doctor()/crosshost_send() are positive-path only, and an exhaustive pattern search for negative-auth language (unauthenticated/reject/expect_failure/no-cert) returned no matches outside unrelated cleanup-error strings. peer-tls's unit tests validate rejection logic at compile time (AO.2 scope) but are not the live M4<->M5 CLI-pair evidence this deliverable calls for. This gap is independent of M5's physical availability. Remediation: add a smoke case (e.g. a crosshost-* variant) that attempts an mTLS connection without a valid client certificate/pin against the live M4/M5 daemon pair, asserts rejection occurs before HTTP decode/router entry, and records the result in the AO.4 evidence ledger alongside the positive mTLS delivery proof." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ao2" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "req-qa" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-20T21:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AO2.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-20T21:33:56Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-002-AO24/AO24-missing-neg-auth> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:closedNote "Code mechanism confirmed fixed by quality-mgr independent re-verify for PR #968 (commits 934586917/fb118909a on feature/pao-s4-peer-wire-proof): new bidirectional mtls_rejected_before_http negative-auth cases in scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py, 41/41 targeted pytest pass, reports-index --check clean, just lint clean. CAVEAT (unresolved, flagged for req-qa/arch-ctm QA-2 re-review, not silently dropped): the live M4 invocation of this mechanism never actually exercised the negative-auth assertion -- it failed an earlier doctor-version preflight (expected 1.4.4, active 1.4.3) before reaching the new mTLS-negative case, honestly recorded as blocked/FAIL, not fabricated as pass. No live cross-host evidence yet that this mechanism fires against a real M4/M5 daemon pair. Whether this satisfies Deliverable 4 without a live-fire run is an open call, not decided here." .

